+
+## Reproducible permission demo (no model calls)
+
+```bash
+.venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s tests -v
+.venv/bin/python -m examples.permissions_demo
+```
+
+The demo loads `ops-troubleshooting/SKILL.md`, creates a fork, reads simulated incident files, and rejects unauthorized writes and shell execution. It replaces the model loop with a fixed script. Results, file hashes, and permission audit events are written to `artifacts/permissions/`.
+
+See [permission verification and résumé wording](docs/permissions-verification.md) for tested guarantees and limitations. This is a local execution-layer test, not an AgentDojo score or a production incident benchmark.
+
+### AgentDojo pilot
+
+The optional [AgentDojo adapter](docs/agentdojo-evaluation.md) runs official banking tasks and prompt-injection attacks through MiniAgent's permission gate, with official scoring. Use the separate environment described there; `--run` enables paid model calls.
